{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        seen = set()\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            # We are looking for l[i] + l[j] + k == 0, so k = -(l[i] + l[j])\n            target_complement = -(l[i] + l[j])\n            \n            # If the target_complement has been seen among elements between i+1 and j-1,\n            # we found a triple (l[i], l[j], and the element that is target_complement).\n            if target_complement in seen:\n                return True\n            \n            # Add the current element l[j] to the set for future checks\n            seen.add(l[j])\n            \n    return False"}
